[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2448469238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2448469238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2448469238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6R8Kz2","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-30T21:40:19Z","updated_at":"2024-10-30T21:40:19Z","body":"The trouble with this sort of modifier is that the strength of the modifier needed is dependent on the brightness of the pixel being calculated. I.e. a modifier of 0.33 may look fine in this test case, but it won't work in other configurations. More importantly, it won't work in cases where brightness varies within the range of the light (for example if the light partially overlaps another light). \r\n\r\nWe discussed this extensively when implementing the Compatibility renderer and agreed that we should leave it up to users to modify the brightness of the light using the energy parameter since there will be no one-size-fits-all solution","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2448469238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2448799291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2448799291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2448799291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6R9bY7","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-31T01:11:10Z","updated_at":"2024-10-31T01:11:29Z","body":"> we should leave it up to users to modify the brightness of the light using the energy parameter since there will be no one-size-fits-all solution\r\n\r\nThis is exactly what this PR is about. It allows doing so without needing a dedicated script on each light node :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nThe PR does *not* change the default appearance of lights when using Compatibility, as the default multiplier is `1.0` and it multiplies the **Energy** property.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2448799291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515409119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2515409119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2515409119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7hjf","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T19:29:06Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T19:31:06Z","body":"\"Rendering method\" and \"renderer\" refer to the same concept and both are valid terms. \"Renderer\" is just slightly friendlier and shorter so we should *prefer* it in general. In this case \"rendering method\" is fine and even makes more sense because `ProjectSettings.rendering/renderer/rendering_method` is referenced.\r\n\r\n(It is a bit unfortunate that we have two names for the same thing, but existing usage was thoroughly mixed between the two, the *engine* calls the rendering methods, \"renderer\" is the nicer term in the abstract and was thoroughly used in the docs, and we weren't going to rename the actual project setting, so here we are 🤷)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515409119/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518153995","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2518153995","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2518153995,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WF_sL","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T17:56:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T17:56:35Z","body":"> I... I am not sure this needs to be configurable per-light. Can't this be an project setting or similar?\r\n\r\nIt *needs* to be configured on a per-light basis for the reason mentioned by clayjohn above. A project setting lacks enough granularity to give a good result in varied scenarios.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2518153995/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608661299","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2608661299","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2608661299,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bfQMz","user":{"login":"Gromph","id":361560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTU2MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/361560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph","html_url":"https://github.com/Gromph","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T01:39:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T01:39:45Z","body":"We added a user display quality option to turn shadows off and on. Then noticed that objects were darker with shadows off.  Merged this pull request, turned lights up to be good with shadows off, then set shadow_light_energy_compatibility  to 0.55 to get brigthness to match with and without shadows.   Looks good now.   So this pull request looks good to me.  Unless there is some way to solve the problem automatically without having to manually adjust shadow_light_energy_compatibility","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608661299/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626214912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2626214912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2626214912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ciNwA","user":{"login":"llama-nl","id":94882246,"node_id":"U_kgDOBafJxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94882246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl","html_url":"https://github.com/llama-nl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T03:19:51Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T03:20:49Z","body":"![20250124_115809](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30b5caa3-c4ba-4913-998b-395a66b28050)\r\n\r\nWhat about the blue tone.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626214912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2640310897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2640310897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2640310897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dX_Jx","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T16:21:00Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T16:21:00Z","body":"> What about the blue tone.\r\n\r\nThe different tone in sky lighting is unrelated to this PR. It can stem from different sources (i.e. different calculations in sky radiance and irradiance map, different way to apply it onto materials, different tonemapping). I would try to isolate what's causing it to see if we can add dedicated properties to better control it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2640310897/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842650352","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-2842650352","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":2842650352,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pb2bw","user":{"login":"llama-nl","id":94882246,"node_id":"U_kgDOBafJxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94882246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl","html_url":"https://github.com/llama-nl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T17:00:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T17:00:19Z","body":"@Calinou Is the work on this PR complete? If so, would it be possible to merge it? This is a significant issue and resolving it would really helpfull. I wonder if you're still working on it?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842650352/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3802372247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-3802372247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":3802372247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7io5iX","user":{"login":"Gromph","id":361560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MTU2MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/361560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph","html_url":"https://github.com/Gromph","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Gromph/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T00:04:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T00:04:43Z","body":"I just upgraded our games from 4.3 to 4.6.  And still have this issue were if shadows are disabled everything gets darker. I had merged this into our 4.3 fork and it fixed it.    Since this was never merged into godot master is there a better solution?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3802372247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5277608959","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98656#issuecomment-5277608959","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98656","id":5277608959,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOpHr_w","user":{"login":"pyhfen","id":304356368,"node_id":"U_kgDOEiQcEA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/304356368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen","html_url":"https://github.com/pyhfen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pyhfen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T07:54:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T07:54:58Z","body":"I personally remove `frag_color.rgb = linear_to_srgb(frag_color.rgb);` & `additive_light_color = linear_to_srgb(additive_light_color);` from `scene.glsl`. Works so much better than this. Shadowed lights and non shadowed lights look the same. Since they look the same i can disable the shadows of distant lights without horrible pop in. Also makes the light blending perfect.\r\nLights on the left cast shadow.\r\n<img width=\"1200\" height=\"780\" alt=\"0dif\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62014a0b-fcca-4b8e-8b28-8dbc7770337d\" />\r\nIt does make everything darker though but i only use the compatibility renderer. Im not interested in switching renderers.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5277608959/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]